<title>RUSSIA: Russian sugarbeet harvest could fall to 17.5 mln T.</title>
<headline>Russian sugarbeet harvest could fall to 17.5 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's sugarbeet harvest is likely to be 17.5-19.0 million tonnes this year after 19.1 million in 1995, Alexander Nechosov, deputy head of the Semsvyokla sugar beet seed producers' association, said on Monday.</p>
<p>Nechosov, quoting Agriculture Ministry data made available to the industry on Friday, said Russian sugar production would fall to 1.85-1.90 million tonnes from 2.06 million in 1995.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
